1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:01,875
The company has $20,000 in the bank.

2
00:00:01,890 --> 00:00:03,315
The owner thinks: fantastic!

3
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,380
Finally, a bonus for myself!

4
00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:07,275
But the accountant says: hold on.

5
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:09,100
Can you take that money? Why not?

6
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:10,935
Here is a key business concept.

7
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,180
Working Capital

8
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:14,355
Put simply,

9
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:15,675
day-to-day business operations

10
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:17,620
need enough funds to keep moving.

11
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:19,420
Money in the bank

12
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:21,520
does not mean you can take it all.

13
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:23,680
All figures are hypothetical.

14
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:24,915
Imagine a small business.

15
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:26,835
Its bank balance is $20,000.

16
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:28,455
But next month it must pay:

17
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:30,340
Payroll: $6,000.

18
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:31,815
Rent: $3,000.

19
00:00:31,830 --> 00:00:33,820
Supplier payments: $8,000.

20
00:00:33,990 --> 00:00:36,040
That totals $17,000.

21
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:37,480
Wait a moment.

22
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:39,615
There is $20,000 in the account.

23
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:42,460
Subtract the $17,000 coming due.

24
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:44,115
Only $3,000 remains.

25
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,915
If the owner takes $10,000,

26
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:48,100
the business may miss its bills.

27
00:00:48,690 --> 00:00:51,160
So look beyond the bank balance.

28
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:53,055
When will cash come in?

29
00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:54,160
When must payments go out?

30
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:55,875
And how much should the business keep

31
00:00:55,890 --> 00:00:57,460
as an emergency cash buffer?

32
00:00:57,570 --> 00:00:59,415
That is why cash planning

33
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,120
matters so much to small businesses.

34
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:02,715
Real businesses, of course,

35
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:05,380
also face taxes, loans and other costs.

36
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:06,880
Remember:

37
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:08,355
Your bank balance shows

38
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:09,640
how much cash you have now.

39
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:11,235
Your cash budget shows

40
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:13,120
whether you can safely spend it.

41
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:15,100
This is Business Through Data.
